# Hook Maker: local/private files (auto-managed)
/.env
/.env.*
!/.env.example
!/.env.sample
!/.env.template
!/.env.dist

# The portable data root: profiles, browser sessions, the proxy pool and logs.
# Created beside the app by design - never tracked.
/data/

# Build outputs. Source and builds are kept apart on purpose: everything under
# build/ is produced by scripts/, never edited, and published through Releases.
/build/

# The self-hosted CI runner and everything it checks out or builds. Kept inside
# the project on purpose - one folder to delete - and never tracked: it holds a
# runner credential, a second copy of this repository, and multi-gigabyte build
# output. Its prerequisites are installed once in the WSL distro and shared.
#
# The Linux runner now lives at the workstation's canonical /srv/ci roots, so
# /.ci-runner/ is kept only so an older checkout stays ignored. The Windows
# runner has no /srv, so it stays project-owned: installation, job workspace
# and download cache all inside this folder, one directory to delete.
/.ci-runner/
/.ci-runner-win/
/.ci-work/
/.ci-cache/

# Icon sizes derived from docs/brand/Logo.png by scripts/make-icons.py.
# The source, the 1024 master and the size the README embeds are tracked; these
# are intermediates that nothing references and that regenerate in a second.
/docs/brand/logo-512.png
/docs/brand/logo-128.png
